  "legalTermsBody": "MUSA is a music player for Android that works with the files on your phone.\n\nAdd-ons: independent programs that you add voluntarily by code, file or repository. They are not part of MUSA and are not included in the app. Their authors are responsible for them, and you are responsible for choosing which ones to install.\n\nThird-party services: MUSA is not affiliated with, sponsored by or endorsed by Apple, Spotify, Deezer, Tidal, Amazon, Qobuz, SoundCloud, YouTube or any other music service. Using a service through an add-on is governed by that service's terms and is the user's responsibility.\n\nContent: MUSA does not host or distribute music or protected content. Only play or save content you have the right to use.\n\nThe beta version may contain errors and is provided as is, without warranties. You can stop using it at any time.",
  "@legalTermsBody": {"description": "Public beta legal flow"},
  "legalPrivacyHeading": "Privacy policy",
  "@legalPrivacyHeading": {"description": "Public beta legal flow"},
  "legalPrivacyBody": "There are no accounts and no ads.\n\nYour library, listening history and settings are stored only on your phone.\n\nDiagnostics: sent only when you ask from Settings, with the report you see before sending it.\n\nAnonymous usage counters: installs, activity and the number of downloads and plays. They include no titles, searches or IP address. You can turn them off with the switch in settings.\n\nAdd-ons you install may connect to their own services; how they handle data depends on each service.",
